# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Linc — one .gitignore, at the repository root.
#
# Merged in M19 from the old Linc/.gitignore when the repo root moved up a
# level (Linc/ became a folder inside the repo instead of being the repo).
# Paths are therefore relative to the ROOT, not to Linc/.
#
# Rule of thumb: build output and machine-local state are ignored; everything
# the product needs to build — including the vendored scrcpy binaries — is not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- OS ---
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# --- IDEs / editors / local agent state ---
.idea/
.vs/
.vscode/
.continue/
.claude/
*.user
*.suo

# --- Secrets and machine-local config (never committed) ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/local.properties
skills-lock.json

# --- The nemo MCP worker (A4) ---
# Not part of the product: it is tooling for the AI that helps build Linc, it
# carries its own API configuration, and it has no business in a public repo.
MCP/

# --- Android / Gradle ---
**/.gradle/
**/build/
**/captures/
**/.kotlin/
*.apk
*.aab
*.keystore
*.jks

# --- .NET / WinUI ---
# Auto-generated VS "open folder" wrapper project (not part of the build)
Linc/DESKTOP/Linc Desktop.sln
Linc/DESKTOP/Linc Desktop.vcxproj
Linc/DESKTOP/Linc Desktop.vcxproj.filters
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/Generated Files/
publish/
*.binlog

# --- scrcpy (vendored) ---
# ONLY the meson build directories. The vendored scrcpy BINARIES the product
# ships with (Linc/SCRCPY/Linc.scrcpy/bin/ - scrcpy.exe, scrcpy-server, SDL2 and
# the ~98 mingw64 DLLs) are deliberately NOT ignored: the desktop app cannot
# mirror without them, and they are the whole point of vendoring scrcpy.
# The un-ignore below MUST come after the "**/bin/" rule above, which would
# otherwise swallow them (it did, until this was caught in M19).
Linc/SCRCPY/**/src/x/
Linc/SCRCPY/**/x/
!Linc/SCRCPY/Linc.scrcpy/bin/
!Linc/SCRCPY/Linc.scrcpy/bin/**

# --- Release output ---
# The shipped artefacts (a 171 MB desktop zip and the APK) ship as GitHub
# Release assets, never as tracked files — GitHub hard-rejects blobs >100 MB.
# M19 moved the real prod/ out of the tree entirely; this is defensive.
prod/
prod.rar
*.rar

# --- Logs / temp ---
*.log
*.tmp

# --- Local-only leftovers ---
docs/task.txt
v1.docs.old/
commit-msg.txt
